# PR preview list generation

When you fill in the **Preview Link(s) & JIRA Ticket** section of a Harness Developer Hub PR, do not list every changed markdown file. Per-page previews are only needed when rendered page content changes.

## Manual commands

```bash
npm run generate-pr-preview-list
```

## Frontmatter-only changes (exclude from preview list)

Skip per-page preview rows when the diff only touches YAML frontmatter, including:

- `redirect_from`
- `title`, `sidebar_label`, `description`
- `sidebar_position`, `slug`, `keywords`, `tags`
- `feature_flags` and other frontmatter keys

These changes do not alter what readers see on the page body, so one Netlify draft URL is enough.

## Include in preview list

Add a preview row when the markdown body changes, including:

- Prose, headings, steps, tables, code blocks
- MDX imports or components in the body
- New doc files with body content

## PR description table

Paste `npm run generate-pr-preview-list` output into the preview section of `.harness/pull_request_template.md`. When every changed doc is frontmatter-only, the script emits a single **Preview URL** row explaining that no per-page previews are needed.

Do not manually enumerate dozens of `Preview: …` rows for redirect or metadata-only PRs.
